    {
      "id": "8a30d120-095c-4743-ad24-84b0bdbdb121",
      "name": "Sticky Note 5041acdd",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        208,
        112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🟢 BEGINNER WORKFLOW\n\n**Concept:** Linear data flow\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Manual trigger starts the workflow\n2. HTTP Request fetches user data from an API\n3. Edit Fields transforms the data (extracts name and email)\n4. Slack sends a notification with the processed data\n\n**Key Learning:**\n- Basic node chaining with .to()\n- Using expressions with expr() to access data\n- Simple data transformation\n- Sending notifications",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "65749450-b7d1-41cb-a130-841b79bcf1db",
      "name": "Sticky Note 47ba1489",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        208,
        752
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🟡 INTERMEDIATE WORKFLOW\n\n**Concept:** Conditional branching and filtering\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Schedule Trigger runs every day at 9 AM\n2. HTTP Request fetches a list of tasks\n3. Filter removes completed tasks\n4. IF node checks priority level\n   - High priority → Send urgent email via Gmail\n   - Normal priority → Send regular Slack message\n\n**Key Learning:**\n- Scheduled automation\n- Filtering data to reduce items\n- Conditional branching with IF node\n- Different actions per branch",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "00f5e12c-6702-425e-9119-817a812f7778",
      "name": "Sticky Note 43894131",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        208,
        1552
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🔴 ADVANCED WORKFLOW\n\n**Concept:** Multi-way routing, parallel execution, and batch processing\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Webhook receives incoming data\n2. Switch routes items by category (urgent/normal/low)\n3. Each category processes differently:\n   - Urgent: Immediate email notification\n   - Normal: Slack notification\n   - Low: Just log the data\n4. Merge combines all results\n5. Aggregate creates summary statistics\n6. Split in Batches processes in groups of 10\n7. Final notification with batch summary\n\n**Key Learning:**\n- Webhook triggers for external integrations\n- Multi-way routing with Switch node\n- Parallel branch execution\n- Merging data from multiple sources\n- Batch processing for large datasets\n- Aggregating data for summaries",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 5
      }
    }
